     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello.<br><br>I am having issues with embedding google motion charts inside html_document, generated by knitr. Here&#39;s a small example:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#080\">```{r, results=&#39;asis&#39;}<br>library(&#39;googleVis&#39;)<br>motion &lt;- gvisMotionChart(data = Fruits, idvar = &#39;Fruit&#39;, timevar = &#39;Year&#39;, <br>                          xvar = &#39;Sales&#39;, yvar = &#39;Expenses&#39;)<br>print(motion, &#39;chart&#39;)<br><br>line &lt;- gvisLineChart(data = Fruits, xvar = &#39;Sales&#39;, yvar = &#39;Expenses&#39;)<br>print(line, &#39;chart&#39;)<br>```</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>The line chart is displaying just fine. The motion chart is showing blank. <br>Running <span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">plot(motion)</span> displays motion chart inside browser just fine, so this is not browser issue (tested output in FF, Chrome, IE). <br>I understand this may be googleVis issue, but would you please take a look?<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(197,200,198);font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:15px;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(29,31,33)\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:10pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;word-break:break-all;margin-